diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 90e3257..23c4d9e 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -29,3 +29,40 @@ Responses:
 
 Messages are created with the bot as `creator`, so the usual callbacks broadcast them
 to connected clients, mark rooms unread, and enqueue web push notifications.
+
+## Webhooks
+
+A bot can optionally store a `webhook_url` (set from the bot form, which labels the
+field "Webhook URL"). Blank values are normalized to `nil`, so saving an empty field
+clears the webhook.
+
+When a message mentions a bot that has a webhook URL and belongs to the room, a
+`Bot::WebhookJob` is enqueued after the message commits. Enqueuing only records the
+job; the HTTP request happens later in the background so posting a message is never
+slowed down by a bot's webhook.
+
+The job POSTs JSON to the bot's webhook:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "mention",
+  "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/<bot_code>/messages" },
+  "message": {
+    "id": 118,
+    "body": { "text": "restart the build please", "html": "<div>…</div>" },
+    "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`message.body.text` strips the bot's own ActionText @-mention, and `room.reply_to`
+is the bot's own posting endpoint for the room. The job handles the bot's reply:
+
+- `200 text/plain` or `text/html` → the body is posted into the room as the bot,
+  broadcasting to clients and enqueueing web push like any other message.
+- `204` → nothing is posted.
+
+Outbound requests are made from `Bot::Webhook`, go through the private-network
+guard, and use connection/read timeouts. Any delivery errors are logged and do not
+change the original message.
